{
 "captions": [
  {
   "at": 98,
   "blocks": [
    "qspi_ctrl",
    "tp_bus"
   ],
   "text": "A fetch from a new address: chip select falls and the controller sends 8 nibbles, address bits 23..0 and the mode byte 0xA0, which keeps the flash in continuous read."
  },
  {
   "at": 114,
   "blocks": [
    "qspi_ctrl"
   ],
   "text": "Four dummy clocks: the flash turns the bus around. uio_oe drops, so the SD pins become inputs."
  },
  {
   "at": 122,
   "blocks": [
    "qspi_ctrl"
   ],
   "text": "Eight data nibbles in. RV32 is little endian and the flash streams ascending addresses, so the first byte on the wire is the least significant; within a byte the high nibble comes first: b 7 0 2 0 0 3 0 is 0x300002b7."
  },
  {
   "at": 138,
   "blocks": [
    "tp_bus",
    "tp_ncore"
   ],
   "text": "imem_rvalid: 0x300002b7 (lui x5, 0x30000) reaches the core."
  },
  {
   "at": 140,
   "blocks": [
    "qspi_ctrl"
   ],
   "text": "The next fetch is sequential, so chip select stayed low and there is no preamble at all: the flash simply clocks out the next word, 8 nibbles instead of 20. This is the streaming that makes straight-line code fast."
  },
  {
   "at": 156,
   "blocks": [
    "tp_ncore"
   ],
   "text": "0x00800313 (addi x6, x0, 8) delivered, 17 clocks after its data phase began."
  }
 ],
